      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can GIRAFFE be run with my own optimizer settings? For our 52 rice leaf samples from the drought trial I want a learning rate of 1e-4, 2,000 iterations and a heavier weight on the PPI term in the loss, because in a pilot the package defaults gave a TF activity matrix that looked over-smoothed and I'd like to see whether these settings change that."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"a learning rate of 1e-4\" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo runs GIRAFFE with its package defaults and passes no settings to it, so \"a learning rate of 1e-4\" cannot be applied. GIRAFFE itself can still run, with its own settings instead -- an alternative, not the setting you asked for.\n\nNo registered workflow can give this as you asked, so none is offered as asked.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
